{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_providers", "label": "Writing a provider (docs/providers.md)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_providers_resolveprovider", "label": "resolveProvider: how a name becomes a running thing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## How a name becomes a running thing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Registry lookup, then await import(name) (.. refused, absolute paths allowed for trying a checkout), accept default export whose kind matches, register under the config name, parse options with the schema, call create. Only 'nothing there' is reported as unknown with alternatives listed; a package that exists but fails to load is reported as exactly that. Context can be a function of the definition so a provider tried by absolute path still logs as its own name."}, {"id": "docs_providers_defineprovider", "label": "defineProvider (identity function for inference)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## The definition", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exists so T is inferred and a package's default export reads as what it is."}, {"id": "docs_providers_providerdefinition", "label": "ProviderDefinition (kind, name, description, schema, create)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## The definition", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_providers_providercontext", "label": "ProviderContext (paths, secrets, log, emit, config)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## The definition", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_providers_apikeyenv_pattern", "label": "apiKeyEnv pattern: name the variable, not the value", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "### A secret of your own", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "context.secrets is a closed set; a provider with its own key takes the env variable's name as an option because parlour copies secrets.env into process.env before any command. Keeps keys out of config.json, lets people rename, and makes parlour secrets status list it. Report a missing key from doctor() rather than throwing in create."}, {"id": "docs_providers_piper_example", "label": "parlour-tts-piper worked example", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## A worked example: Piper as a voice", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Renders to a temp file rather than stdout so a stray log line from piper cannot end up inside the WAV. Throwing from render is how a voice fails; core's FallbackTextToSpeech handles it so the provider needs no fallback of its own."}, {"id": "docs_providers_esm_and_peer_dependency", "label": "type: module and parlour as peer dependency", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## A worked example: Piper as a voice", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Parlour loads packages with import(), and a CommonJS default export is not module.exports. parlour is a peer dependency because the definition is imported from it and there must be exactly one copy. Against a checkout, a file: devDependency satisfies the peer and the link must stay in place at run time because the import is real."}, {"id": "docs_providers_integration_interface", "label": "Integration interface (tools, promptContext, gate, close)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## An integration", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Selected by being a key under integrations; the block replaces the default rather than adding, so a hand-written one must keep home-assistant and connectors. tools() is called once at assembly so a connection opened there stays open; close() shuts it."}, {"id": "docs_providers_definetool", "label": "defineTool and short tool names", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## An integration", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every tool description sits in the local model's context on every turn, so a package with forty tools makes every answer slower; keep names stable and short."}, {"id": "docs_providers_testing_fakes", "label": "parlour/testing fakes for every port", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## Testing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each fake records what it was asked so a provider can run through the same VoiceSession and Router the built-ins are tested against. Providers needing hardware or a model are not unit tested; each has a doctor() instead, which is what a person sees when the thing does not work."}, {"id": "docs_providers_platform_picked_providers", "label": "secrets and service picked by platform", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## The other kinds", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not named in config; adding a systemd ServiceManager means registering it in providers/service/index.ts, which makes it a pull request rather than a package."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_providers_resolveprovider", "target": "docs_providers_providerdefinition", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## How a name becomes a running thing", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_providers_resolveprovider", "target": "docs_providers_providercontext", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## How a name becomes a running thing", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_providers_resolveprovider", "target": "docs_architecture_provider_registry", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## How a name becomes a running thing", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_providers_resolveprovider", "target": "packages_parlour_src_core_providers_resolveprovider", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## How a name becomes a running thing", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_providers_defineprovider", "target": "docs_providers_providerdefinition", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## The definition", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_providers_defineprovider", "target": "packages_parlour_src_core_providers_defineprovider", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## The definition", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_providers_providerdefinition", "target": "docs_architecture_ports", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/providers.md", "source_location": "## The other kinds", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_providers_providercontext", "target": "docs_architecture_events_stream", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/provide